methods.explanation:
Write both numbers as multiples of the same power of \(10\). By the meaning of negative exponents,
\[
10^{-49}=\frac{1}{10^{49}}
=\frac{10}{10^{50}}
=10\cdot10^{-50}.
\]
Their difference is therefore
\[
10^{-49}-2\cdot10^{-50}
=(10-2)\cdot10^{-50}
=8\cdot10^{-50}.
\]
This difference is positive, so the first exceeds the second by \(8\cdot10^{-50}\), choice \(\mathrm{C}\).
